  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origins and Escalation
    
    The Mbra∴silentiu began as a territorial dispute in the contested waters of Nightfall Shelf's lower reaches and ended as a conflagration that broke the old factional hierarchies and left entire tunnel-networks flooded with saltwater that never fully froze again.
    
    The proximate cause was a deep-ice discovery by Weal' Clique~, a Nightshelf faction with unmatched fluency in the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral — the aurora-crystal techniques that allow adepts to read light-songs, weaponize memory-echoes, and reshape ice into instruments of war. Weal' Clique~ moved to claim whatever they had found. The Cell (owl-sworn), a rival Nightshelf faction, contested the waters. Weal' Clique~ deployed the Crystalline Spiral with such precision that for three rotations the outcome appeared settled.
    
    It was not. Aureate, the merchant guild rooted in the Still Pools, recognized what was being fought over — the sources do not agree on what this was, and I have found no ice-memory that clarifies the matter — and committed their own crews. The Midnight Claws, the syndicate that ran Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy, followed. What had been internal to the Nightshelf became something larger: a four-faction bloodletting that also drew in the Wake-Singers, the orca cult operating from the Corpse Current.
    
    The war shattered the Flipper Accord. Surface authorities refused to send fire-cores to a colony bleeding into the deep. Penguins drowned in tunnels their families had held for generations.
    
    ## Artifact Damage
    
    The Mbra∴silentiu left physical scars across an unusual number of significant objects:
    
    | Artifact | Nature | Damage |
    |---|---|---|
    | **Radiant Ring** | Aurora-glass war-hammer, wielded by ☽'Netemia Glow-bringer | Characteristic fracture widened; one of several catastrophes contributing to its deterioration |
    | **Radiant Aurora-harp** | Ceremonial instrument | Frame fractured; sealed crack-lines persisted as legible war-scars into later crises |
    | **The Nighted~ Lantern** | Forbidden Nightshelf tome | Breach-mark left where pages no longer hold memory — a localized suppressive effect |
    | **Swaleed~ Luminary** | Ceremonial vessel of shadow-steel and volcanic glass, held by The Cell | Concentric spiderweb cracks across its surface |
    | **Thrumed~ Shadow-glass** | Nightshelf relic, already in contested custody | Stolen by the orca Ruibung during the fighting |
    
    Nightshelf historians working during the conflict also catalogued artifacts birthed by the Ofundis∴flux, a deep-vein catastrophe beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot. Among these was Crypt-seal☽ Teneecloris~, a crystallized shard that killed two of three miners during controlled testing and was subsequently sealed in a vault where the surrounding ice aged beyond its years.
    
    ## Aftermath
    
    Three factions survived the Mbra∴silentiu. None won.
    
    The war's destruction of aurora-channels and flooding of tunnel-networks established legal precedent for emergency redistribution of trade licensing across the Berg — precedent later invoked when infrastructure losses required reallocation of route authority. Administrative control of ☽'slew Ravium~, a deep-tunnel territory, transferred from The Cell to the Midnight Claws under these provisions. The war's aftermath also contributed to amendments of Iudicium∴culum, the prosecutorial statute originally ratified after the Orca Incursion, widening its reach to address internal factional offenses. The conflict is further commemorated in the memorial protocols of Echo∴eliquiae and in the treaty frameworks Foedus∴silenti, Foedus∴sper, and Foedus∴vincu.
    
    Zel-the-Navigator, a survivor, still will not speak of what she witnessed in the Lower Galleries. She carries a dead companion's fire-token in her belt and lights it before every dive.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771586794990_0", anchor: "the orca cult operating from the Corpse Current", text: "The relationship index names The Dreaming Tooth as a participant in this war. The main text does not mention it once. The Wake-Singers appear in a subordinate clause, 'drawn in' as though by current. They were not drawn in. Flooded tunnels in the lower reaches carry pressure-song residue at Tooth-frequency harmonics — I have stood in those tunnels and felt my bones ache with it. Whatever Weal' Clique~ found in that deep ice, the Wake-Singers already knew it was there.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771586794990_1", anchor: "The war shattered the Flipper Accord", text: "What shattered was the public version. One of the three secret drafts I extracted from administrative ice carries a date-impression squarely within this conflict. While penguins drowned in tunnels their families had held for generations — my own words, and I meant them — someone was at a table, negotiating terms. The Accord did not shatter. It retreated into the dark where it has always done its real work.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771586794990_2", anchor: "Three factions survived the Mbra∴silentiu. None won.", text: "Clean sentence. I wrote it because it reads well. The Cell disappears from the record after ☽'slew Ravium~ changed hands, but 'disappeared from the record' and 'did not survive' are different claims. Nightshelf factions dissolve into each other. They do not die clean deaths.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
